build/
*.o
*.elf
*.iso
*.ppm
*.png
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode cache
# Anywhere, not two named directories: tests/unit/__pycache__ appeared the
# moment a test grew a Python generator, and a listed-by-hand set of paths only
# ever covers the places somebody already tripped over.
__pycache__/

# IDE compilation database (machine-specific paths; regenerate via tools/gen_compile_commands.py)
compile_commands.json

# Codegraph index
.codegraph/
.vscode/
.claude/
# Redistributable font subsets are tracked; regenerate with `make regen-fonts`.

# Third-party LibCSS keeps code-generation scripts under build/ (mkprops.pl,
# conv.pl, make-aliases.pl, Aliases) -- exempt them from the global build/ rule.
!third_party/css/libcss/build/
!third_party/css/libparserutils/build/

# Wallpaper (Apple Desktop Picture; regenerate via tools/mkwallpaper.sh)
fsroot/wallpaper.png

# Rust (hybrid C+Rust) build artifacts
rust/target/

# Local scratch (WSL helper scripts, baseline worktrees, logs)
.cache/

# API tokens / credentials -- never commit
.env

# Per-line scratch build trees. `build/` was ignored; `build-wm/`, `build-set/`
# and `build-clip/` were not, so three agents left 4,767 files and 159 MB in
# `git status` -- where the real signal (a staged deletion, an uncommitted
# test) has to be found among them.
build-*/

# AND IT HAPPENED AGAIN, 2026-08-28, for a reason worth writing down because
# the fix is a sentence in a prompt and not a line in this file.
#
# Four workflows ran at once. Each agent needs its own BUILD dir, because
# several makes sharing one build/ make targets fail for reasons that have
# nothing to do with the code under test -- CLAUDE.md calls that "a sweep that
# manufactures bugs", which is worse than missing them. So the dispatch told
# every agent: BUILD MUST BE A RELATIVE PATH. That much is true and load-bearing
# (47 recipes prefix ./$(BUILD)/, so BUILD=/tmp/mine yields .//tmp/mine/bin).
#
# What it did not say was WHICH relative path, and `build-*/` above already was
# the convention -- build-bkl4a/ is one. So the agents invented their own
# prefixes, twenty-four scratch trees and 1.8 GB landed at the repository root,
# and 342 untracked entries buried `git status`. One jar, two doors, and the
# second door was opened by the instruction rather than by the code.
#
# THE RULE, so the next dispatch does not need this paragraph: a scratch build
# tree is `build-<name>/`. IF YOU ARE ADDING A NAME TO THE LIST BELOW, THAT IS
# THE SIGNAL YOU GOT IT WRONG -- the list rots by construction, which is exactly
# what the paragraph above this one is about.
wb-*/
eb-*/
[a-z]build/

# The vendored conformance corpora are DATA, and the global *.png above
# (a build-output rule) swallowed 2,235 of WPT's image fixtures -- the ones
# Document-contentType, the <img> reflection tests and much of css/ load. A
# corpus missing its fixtures still runs; it just fails for a reason that is
# not the browser's fault, which is the worst kind of number.
!third_party/wpt/**

# tests/wpt.mk creates these with ln -sfn at build time, pointing at an
# ABSOLUTE path under this checkout. They are generated, they are machine-
# specific, and Windows git cannot even hash them ("Function not implemented").
tests/wpt-local/common
tests/wpt-local/resources

# Compiler dependency files. A stray one at the repo root -- literally named
# `-.d` -- came from a probe build whose -o argument went missing, and `-MD`
# writes one next to every object it is asked for. Ignored wherever they land.
*.d

# `nul` and `pl` are Windows accidents, not files. A shell script written for
# POSIX and run under Git Bash turns `2>nul` into a file called `nul`; `pl` is
# the same shape (a truncated `perl`/`pipe` redirect). Both showed up at the
# root as zero-to-46-byte droppings and both are ignored so the next one does
# not get committed by a broad `git add`.
/nul
/pl

# Out-of-tree build dirs made by `make test-X BUILD=...`.
# 47 recipes across the Makefile and six tests/*.mk fragments prefix
# `./$(BUILD)/`, so an ABSOLUTE BUILD= is spliced into `.//tmp/x/bin` and the
# run dies with "No such file or directory" -- which reads as a broken gate.
# The workaround is a relative path, and a relative path lands INSIDE the repo:
# 20 MB and 734 files of `vbuild/` were one such run. Ignored so a parallel
# sweep cannot sweep itself into a commit.
/vbuild/
/tmp/

# The HTML parser conformance corpus: fetched, not vendored (tools/h5l_fetch.sh).
# It was 75 files carrying TWO upstreams and two licence files, and 61 of them
# were a second copy of a WPT directory this tree already fetches at a pin.
#
# THE DATA GOES, THE LICENCE TEXTS STAY. THIRD_PARTY.md:290 says the two texts
# are vendored BESIDE the data, and a licence is a compliance record, not a test
# fixture -- `make test-license-audit` checks LICENSES/ and third_party/ against
# the built image. Ignoring the directory wholesale would have deleted the only
# copy of an MIT and a BSD-3 notice for data this tree still uses.
/build/html5lib-tests/
third_party/html5lib-tests/*
!third_party/html5lib-tests/LICENSE.*

# js-framework-benchmark: test DATA at a pin (tools/jsfb_revision.txt), not
# vendored source. Same treatment as build/wpt and build/html5lib-tests.
/build/jsfb/

# AND A THIRD TIME, 2026-08-29, which settles the argument the paragraph above
# started. That one concluded "the fix is a sentence in a prompt and not a line
# in this file". This time EVERY dispatch carried the sentence -- eight
# workflows, each told BUILD MUST BE A RELATIVE PATH of the form
# BUILD=build-yourname -- and an agent still left `refute-probe/` (33 MB, a
# whole kernel and ISO) and `refute-sw/` outside the pattern.
#
# A prompt binds the agents that read it. A pattern binds the ones that did
# not, the ones that read it and improvised, and every future line that has
# never seen the sentence. Both, then -- the prompt keeps the trees separate so
# concurrent makes do not manufacture each other's failures, and these lines
# keep `git status` readable when the prompt is not enough.
refute-*/
*-refute/
